{
 "encounter_id": "00953",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good to see you again, Dana. It's about three weeks since we last spoke. How have things been since the accident? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. Not great. I keep having these, I guess flashbacks? I see the truck, the lights, I'm back on the road."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How often?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A couple of times a week. It started... I don't know. A month after? Maybe two? I can't really say."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And at night?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Nightmares. Bad ones. I wake up sweating, and I'm scared to go back to sleep."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had any thoughts of harming yourself?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. No, nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Are you drinking more than you used to?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, not really. A glass of wine, same as always."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's go through your medications."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sertraline, 50 mg, once a day. Prazosin, 1 mg, at night, for the nightmares. And ibuprofen, 400 mg, when my leg aches."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you take the sertraline every day?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Every day. Well, most days. I forget it if I'm in a rush."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. Thanks for being straight with me. Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Penicillin. Hives."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any other health problems?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Anxiety, I guess. Before all this."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And the accident, you had surgery on the leg, I believe?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yeah. A rod put in my left shin, four months ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How's the leg? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Better. Sore if I walk a long way. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me look at you, Dana. You seem restless, shifting a lot in the chair.",
   "pause": 8.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yeah. I can't sit still. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain or palpitations between the flashbacks?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing, I'm fine between them."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's helpful. What you're describing, the flashbacks, the nightmares and the jumpiness, fits post-traumatic stress after the accident."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "PTSD? Like soldiers? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's not just soldiers. Anyone who has been through something frightening can have it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it going to go away? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "For most people, yes, with treatment. Keep taking your sertraline every day. It works best taken regularly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll set an alarm. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good idea. I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And if it gets worse before then, ring the clinic. Don't wait. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  }
 ],
